# .trivyignore - KubeSentinel Security Scan Exceptions
# ==============================================================================
# This file documents narrowly scoped exceptions for third-party security agents
# and telemetry collectors operating in the KubeSentinel Kubernetes cluster.
#
# Exception Policy:
# 1. Project application code and workloads (edge-api, edge-worker, redis) must
#    have ZERO exceptions and ZERO fixable HIGH/CRITICAL findings.
# 2. Third-party infrastructure daemons (Falco modern_ebpf, Fluent Bit) require
#    specific elevated host and kernel access to fulfill their monitoring roles.
# 3. No findings are silenced without documented justification and scope.
# ==============================================================================

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Falco Modern eBPF Runtime Security Sensor
# Namespace: security-agents | Pod/DaemonSet: falco
# Justification: Falco requires host kernel visibility to capture system calls,
# trace execve/connect events, and correlate process activity with Kubernetes pods.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Container running with 'privileged' flag (AVD-KSV-0012 / KSV012 / KSV-0017)
# Required for modern_ebpf driver to attach eBPF probes to kernel tracepoints in k3d.
AVD-KSV-0012
KSV012
KSV-0017

# hostPath volumes mounted (AVD-KSV-0023 / KSV023 / KSV-0006 / KSV-0121)
# Required to access /proc, /etc, and containerd socket (/run/containerd/containerd.sock)
# to enrich raw kernel events with container and process metadata.
AVD-KSV-0023
KSV023
KSV-0006
KSV-0121

# Allow privilege escalation enabled (AVD-KSV-0001 / KSV0001)
# Required because privileged container must retain root privileges to manage eBPF maps.
AVD-KSV-0001
KSV0001

# Root filesystem is not read-only (AVD-KSV-0014 / KSV014)
# Falco daemon writes dynamic state, rule caches, and probe diagnostics at runtime.
AVD-KSV-0014
KSV014

# Container running as root (AVD-KSV-0020 / KSV020)
# Kernel eBPF probe attachment requires UID 0 on the host node.
AVD-KSV-0020
KSV020
KSV-0118

# Linux capabilities not dropped (AVD-KSV-0043 / KSV043)
# Requires CAP_SYS_ADMIN / CAP_BPF / CAP_SYS_RESOURCE for modern_ebpf subsystem.
AVD-KSV-0043
KSV043

# Host PID namespace enabled (AVD-KSV-0010 / KSV010)
# Required to correlate container PIDs with host kernel thread IDs.
AVD-KSV-0010
KSV010

# Host network namespace enabled (AVD-KSV-0009 / KSV0009)
# Required for network connection tracing across container interfaces.
AVD-KSV-0009
KSV0009

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. Fluent Bit Telemetry Log Collector
# Namespace: observability | Pod/DaemonSet: fluent-bit
# Justification: In standard Kubernetes, container stdout/stderr logs are stored
# on the host node at /var/log/pods/. Fluent Bit mounts /var/log read-only to ingest
# application and security event logs into Elasticsearch.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Storage of container logs requires host /var/log volume mount (AVD-KSV-0018 / KSV018)
# Fluent Bit mounts /var/log as read-only.
AVD-KSV-0018
KSV018
